  "term": "hippocampus",
  "definition": "The hippocampus is a curved band of gray matter that lies along the full floor of the temporal horn of the lateral ventricle. It is one part of the hippocampal formation, together with the hippocampus proper, subiculum, and dentate gyrus; some descriptions also include the entorhinal cortex.",
