      "reasons": [
        "The packet defines the hippocampus as a curved elevation of gray matter extending the length of the temporal horn floor, but it does not support the added claim that the hippocampus itself is “one part of the hippocampal formation.” It only says the hippocampus proper, subiculum, and dentate gyrus constitute that formation.",
